    "theorem": "FiniteFourierUpperBoundAudit.finite_fourier_upper_bound_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem finite_fourier_upper_bound_certificate : (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (f : G → ℂ), (∑ ψ : AddChar G ℂ, Complex.normSq (rawFourier f ψ)) = (Fintype.card G : ℝ)*(∑ x, Complex.normSq (f x))) ∧ (∀ (S : Type) [Fintype S] (q r : PMF S), totalVariation q r=l1Distance q r/2 ∧ 0 ≤ totalVariation q r ∧ totalVariation q r ≤ 1 ∧ (∀ A : Finset S, abs (eventMass q A-eventMass r A) ≤ totalVariation q r) ∧ eventMass q (positiveEvent q r)-eventMass r (positiveEvent q r)=totalVariation q r) ∧ (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (q r : PMF G), differenceEnergy q r=(Fintype.card G : ℝ)*(∑ x, (weight q x-weight r x)^2) ∧ (l1Distance q r)^2 ≤ differenceEnergy q r ∧ (totalVariation q r)^2 ≤ (1/4 : ℝ)*differenceEnergy q r) ∧ (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (x : G), (uniformLaw G x).toReal=1/(Fintype.card G : ℝ)) ∧ (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (A : Finset G), eventMass (uniformLaw G) A=(A.card : ℝ)/(Fintype.card G : ℝ)) ∧ (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (ψ : AddChar G ℂ), (ψ=0 → complexExpectation (uniformLaw G) ψ=1) ∧ (ψ ≠ 0 → complexExpectation (uniformLaw G) ψ=0)) ∧ (∀ (G : Type) [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (q : PMF G), differenceEnergy q (uniformLaw G)=nontrivialEnergy q ∧ (totalVariation q (uniformLaw G))^2 ≤ (1/4 : ℝ)*nontrivialEnergy q) ∧ (∀ (I G : Type) [Fintype I] [Fintype G] [AddCommGroup G] (q : PMF I) (a : I → G) (t : ℕ) (x : G), (totalVariation (kernelLaw q (fun i y => y+a i) t x) (uniformLaw G))^2 ≤ (1/4 : ℝ)*walkSpectralEnergy q a t ∧ ∀ A : Finset G, (abs (eventMass (kernelLaw q (fun i y => y+a i) t x) A-(A.card : ℝ)/(Fintype.card G : ℝ)))^2 ≤ (1/4 : ℝ)*walkSpectralEnergy q a t) ∧ (l1Distance (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2)) (uniformLaw (ZMod 2))=1 ∧ totalVariation (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2)) (uniformLaw (ZMod 2))=1/2 ∧ nontrivialEnergy (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2))=1) ∧ ((totalVariation (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2)) (uniformLaw (ZMod 2)))^2 = (1/4 : ℝ)*nontrivialEnergy (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2))) ∧ (¬ (l1Distance (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2)) (uniformLaw (ZMod 2)))^2 ≤ (1/4 : ℝ)*nontrivialEnergy (PMF.pure (0 : ZMod 2))) ∧ (∀ c : ℝ, (∀ q : PMF (ZMod 2), (totalVariation q (uniformLaw (ZMod 2)))^2 ≤ c*nontrivialEnergy q) → (1/4 : ℝ) ≤ c)",
    "decl_sha256": "8e1b8c3254622300cf9d726f5eff360ee88e895237fc9e27aedcf53dc96b175b",
    "scope": "Finite-abelian Upper Bound Lemma with actual finite normalized PMFs and genuine uniform law. Finite complex Plancherel derived from character orthogonality, no supplied energy premise. Actual fullL1 and halfL1 are defined from actual point probabilities; halfL1 is in[0,1], bounds every event and is attained by the actual positive-difference event. Actual probability-difference Parseval gives fullL1^2<=difference character energy and halfL1^2<=energy/4. Actual uniform coefficients and probability normalization remove the trivial character. Applying the actual iid character-moment law gives halfL1(walk,uniform)^2 and every-event squared error <=nontrivial normSq(eigenvalue)^t sum/4, for all finite abelian groups/all times/starts. Actual ZMod2 pointmass/uniform has fullL1=1, halfL1=1/2 and nontrivial energy1: direct mixed-normalization bound negation, correct quarter equality and quarter constant necessity. This is a normalization control, not a qualified-source refutation. Original1981 uses fullL1, author1987 report/Hildebrand use halfL1; exact selected primary scopes/versions credited. Standard foundations/default limits; no holes/custom axioms/native evaluation/raised limits/global flags/waivers/native experiment/paid compute/upload. General nonabelian matrix version, canonical measure-tvDist conversion and stronger expected random-support spectral averaging remain open. No novelty claim.",
